# Agent runtime (platform)

Full map: **`docs/AGENT_RUNTIME.md`**.

## Non-negotiables

- Claude = **Agent SDK `query()`** via `askClaude` → `ClaudeRuntime` (`lib/claude-runtime.ts`). Default `CLAUDE_RUNTIME=sdk` (bundled Claude Code CLI + OAuth; coding tools disabled). `cli` = hotfix `claude -p`. Not Anthropic Messages API. Vision on SDK path uses explicit `cli_vision_fallback` (logged). No `maxTurns` cap — stop is `timeoutMs` / AbortSignal. `error_max_turns` with text/tools is not a customer timeout.
- Customer tools = in-process MCP `mcp__platform__*` + `canUseTool` (host still executes book/collect in `conversation.ts`). CLI hotfix keeps the text `<tool_call>` protocol.
- Within a turn: **one session** — tenant reply model keeps a single `--resume` id (`lib/turn-claude-sessions.ts`). Tool follow-ups continue that session (no Haiku hop). Mid-turn prompt activate clears the resume id and aborts in-flight Claude (`AbortSignal`).
- Process hygiene: CLI spawn is a detached process group; abort/timeout kills the group and logs if pid is alive after 2s. `CLAUDE_WARMUP_ON_START` → `runtime.warmup()` (does not arm quota circuit, does not take IG/meta semaphore). Health-check warns on orphan `claude` (ppid 1) without failing.
- Tenant reply model = **sonnet \| opus** only (`normalizeClaudeReplyModel`). The same model handles first spawn and tool follow-ups. Haiku is warmup / usage probe only.
- Tenant timezone = `agent_config.timezone` (default `Europe/Kyiv`). Session clock, working hours, and BeautyPro free_time day bounds use this IANA zone — not the server’s (often DE).
- CRM only via `getCrmAdapter` + `resolveCrmProvider(action)` — never HTTP in `conversation.ts`.
- Platform capability map lives in `lib/platform-capabilities-prompt.ts` — inject into **meta-agent** and **insights (AI-помічник)**. Keep in sync when changing modes/tools/CRM.
- Agent modes: `sales` | `leadgen` | `booking` | **`general`** (union of the three). New tools go into the specialized builder only — general picks them up via `mergeToolsByName` (see `.cursor/rules/agent-mode-general.mdc`).
- Spawn CWD is isolated (`claude-spawn-cwd`) — tenant disk `CLAUDE.md` is **not** the customer system prompt; DB `system_prompts` + runtime injections are.
- Telegram manager alerts are **side effects**, not a customer-facing tool. Product order cards are notify-only (no approve/decline). Handoff: one escalation card, then **no** per-message forwards; one SLA reminder after `managerSlaHoursBusiness` working hours without a manager reply. After `sessionFreshnessDays` of silence, bot **and** handoff threads close and a new conversation starts.
- Native Instagram app replies arrive as Meta `is_echo` on a **separate** tenant route (`/webhooks/instagram/echo`). Inbound still skips echoes. Admin labels them `ig_native_echo` («Менеджер · Instagram»). No Claude on that path.
- Claude customer history is the **tenant civil day** of the current conversation (or from conversation start if it began today), then **after the last completed order/visit today** if several happened. Not a hard last-30 cut. Offered booking slots persist on `Conversation.bookingOffer` (~2h) with per-slot master ids and are injected as «Запропоновані вікна». BeautyPro and CleverBOX book use full CRM ids from that offer (truncated prefixes / names are expanded or refused).
- Client **displayName** is the person name (chat, or a person-like IG profile name). Headlines in `igFullName` are not ПІБ.
- Greeting: first bot outbound in a UUID introduces. Hard «do not re-greet» applies only **that salon civil day** (and ongoing checkout). A new calendar day in the same UUID (salon TZ, e.g. 23:00 → 09:00) injects «Новий календарний день салону» and allows a tenant-prompt greeting; it does not force a full re-intro. `sessionFreshnessDays` still opens a new UUID.

